//? Title: Rice coding: actual quotients, remainders and conditional lengths
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Encode nonnegative integers as prefix-decodable bit words when small values are
common. Rice specializes Golomb coding to a power-of-two model. Actual native
emission and parse histories replace the report-local encoder. The original
eight integers and finite geometric-weight study remain.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For M=2^k, n=qM+r with 0<=r<M. The producer emits q ones, zero, then k remainder
bits:
$$ L_k(n)=\lfloor n/2^k\rfloor+1+k. $$
\alttext(The actual word has unary quotient, one terminator and k remainder bits.)
The original weights are w_n=2^(-n/8) on n=0,...,299 only. The plotted
conditional expectation is sum(w_n L_k(n))/sum(w_n), obtained from actual
emitted spans. It is neither the untruncated geometric expectation nor a random
compression experiment. Model k and decoded count are external metadata.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/rice_coding_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = a::rice_encode_trace({8}, 2);
    auto d = a::rice_decode_trace(t.bits, 2, 1);
    const auto &w = t.words[0];
    std::print("Actual value {}, quotient {}, remainder {}, span length {}, parsed value {}.\n",
               w.value, w.quotient, w.remainder, w.end - w.begin,
               d.words[0].value);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         std::format("Actual n={} and k=2", w.value));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual q={}, r={}", w.quotient,
                                     w.remainder));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual emitted bits {}", w.end - w.begin));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/rice_coding_tiny.svg");
}
```
